  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 330 PM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nSeasonable and mostly dry weather through the rest of the week:\n\nFollowing the strong cold front, appreciably cold air is\nactually not forecast. This is largely due to the mid-level low\nstalling out to our north after the wave exits, with zonal jet\nflow filling in behind. Therefore, temperatures are forecast to\nbe rather seasonable with highs ranging from the upper 50s to\nmiddle 60s and lows in the lower 30s to lower 40s on Wednesday\nthrough the rest of the week.\n\nAnother wave is forecast to move through the area Thursday which\ncould bring some rain (15-30% chance), but with the preceding \ncold front locking appreciable moisture to the Gulf, any \nprecipitation is expected to be light.",
